# Visual Studio SSIS designer reload crash

Editing `.dtsx`, `.dtproj`, `.params`, or `.conmgr` on disk while the file is open in Visual Studio SSDT triggers a reload prompt that hangs or crashes Visual Studio. The user then has to kill `devenv.exe`.

## Before changing those files

1. Tell the user to **close the package and project designer tabs in Visual Studio** (Solution Explorer can stay open).
2. Wait for them to confirm it is closed.
3. Only then write the files.

Do not silently patch a package they are likely debugging in Visual Studio.

## If they still get the reload prompt

Tell them: click **No / Ignore** (do not reload), close the package **without saving**, then reopen it from Solution Explorer so Visual Studio reads the disk copy.

## Prefer designer-safe changes

When a change is a few property values, tell them the exact Visual Studio clicks instead of rewriting the `.dtsx`.
